Q: Java servlet download filename special characters A: <p>I found a solution that worked in all browsers I have installed (<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_Explorer_8" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Internet Explorer 8</a>, Firefox 16, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opera_%28web_browser%29" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Opera</a> 12, and Chrome 22).</p>
<p>It's based on the fact that browsers expect a value in the filename parameter that is encoded in the browser's native encoding, if no (different) encoding is specified.</p>
<p>Usually, the browser's native encoding is UTF-8 (Firefox, Opera, and Chrome). But Internet Explorer's native encoding is <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Windows-1250" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Windows-1250</a>.</p>
<p>So if we put a value into the filename parameter that is encoded by UTF-8/Windows-1250 according to the user's browser, it should work. At least, it works for me.</p>
<pre><code>String fileName = &quot;árvíztűrőtükörfúrógép.xls&quot;;

String userAgent = request.getHeader(&quot;user-agent&quot;);
boolean isInternetExplorer = (userAgent.indexOf(&quot;MSIE&quot;) &gt; -1);

try {
    byte[] fileNameBytes = fileName.getBytes((isInternetExplorer) ? (&quot;windows-1250&quot;) : (&quot;utf-8&quot;));
    String dispositionFileName = &quot;&quot;;
    for (byte b: fileNameBytes) dispositionFileName += (char)(b &amp; 0xff);

    String disposition = &quot;attachment; filename=\&quot;&quot; + dispositionFileName + &quot;\&quot;&quot;;
    response.setHeader(&quot;Content-disposition&quot;, disposition);
} catch(UnsupportedEncodingException ence) {
    // ... handle exception ...
}
</code></pre>
<p>Of course, this is tested only on browsers mentioned above, and I cannot guarantee on 100% that this will work in any browser all time.</p>
<p><strong>Note #1 (@fallen)</strong>:</p>
<p>It's not correct to use the URLEncoder.encode() method. Despite the method's name, it doesn't encode the string into <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percent-encoding" rel="nofollow noreferrer">URL encoding</a>, but it does encode into form-encoding. (Form-encoding is quite similar to URL encoding, and in a lot of cases, it produces same results. But there are some differences. For example, the space character ' ' is encoded differently: '+' instead of '%20')</p>
<p>For a correct URL encoded string, you should use the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniform_Resource_Identifier" rel="nofollow noreferrer">URI</a> class:</p>
<pre><code>URI uri = new URI(null, null, &quot;árvíztűrőtükörfúrógép.xls&quot;, null);
System.out.println(uri.toASCIIString());
</code></pre>

Q: How to programmatically hide a Bootstrap Offcanvas component with JavaScript and Blazor? A: <p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/users/943435/yogi">@Yogi</a> answered my question. I don't need any JavaScript I just needed to add <code>data-bs-dismiss=&quot;offcanvas&quot;</code> to my list items. Here's how it should look</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>  &lt;li class=&quot;list-group-item @ActiveFilter(item)&quot;&gt;
    &lt;a @onclick=&quot;@(e =&gt; ButtonClicked(item))&quot;
         type=&quot;button&quot; data-bs-dismiss=&quot;offcanvas&quot; id=&quot;@item.ButtonId&quot;&gt;
        @item.Value &lt;small&gt;@item.Title&lt;/small&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;
  &lt;/li&gt;
</code></pre>

Q: How do I fix Blocked CORS with Firebase Hosting? A: <p>For 2nd Generation (v2) Functions</p>
<p>For new or updated functions using the v2 SDK, you can set the <code>cors</code> option directly in the function definition:</p>
<pre><code>const { onRequest } = require(&quot;firebase-functions/v2/https&quot;);

exports.foo = onRequest({
  cors: [&quot;https://subdomain.mydomain.com&quot;, &quot;https://*.web.app&quot;] // Add your specific domain(s)
}, (req, res) =&gt; {
  // Your function logic here
  res.status(200).send(&quot;Response data&quot;);
});
</code></pre>

Q: Why is $(SolutionDir) undefined in dotnet CLI? A: <p>Perhaps use a helper and search for the .sln file i.e.</p>
<pre><code>using System.IO;

public static class SolutionHelper
{
    public static string GetSolutionDirectory()
    {
        var directory = new DirectoryInfo(
            Path.GetDirectoryName(System.Reflection.Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly().Location));

        while (directory != null &amp;&amp; !directory.GetFiles(&quot;*.sln&quot;).Any())
        {
            directory = directory.Parent;
        }

        return directory?.FullName ?? throw new DirectoryNotFoundException(&quot;Solution file not found&quot;);
    }
}
</code></pre>
